  "context_pill": "A.Y. 2026-27 Tax Computation",
  "example_summary": "Computation of tax liability for Mr. Arjun across three different age tiers under the opted-out Section 115BAC regime.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Optional Tax Regime Slabs for Resident Individuals\n\n| Resident Individual Category | Age Threshold | Basic Exemption Limit | Applicable Tax Slab Rates |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Normal Individual** | Below 60 years | ₹ 2,50,000 | Up to ₹ 2.5L: Nil<br>₹ 2.5L - ₹ 5L: 5%<br>₹ 5L - ₹ 10L: 20%<br>Above ₹ 10L: 30% |\n| **Senior Citizen** | 60 years to 79 years | ₹ 3,00,000 | Up to ₹ 3L: Nil<br>₹ 3L - ₹ 5L: 5%<br>₹ 5L - ₹ 10L: 20%<br>Above ₹ 10L: 30% |\n| **Super Senior Citizen** | 80 years or above | ₹ 5,00,000 | Up to ₹ 5L: Nil<br>₹ 5L - ₹ 10L: 20%<br>Above ₹ 10L: 30% |\n\n\n### Core Statutory Conditions\n\n* **Residential Status Mandatory**: Enhanced basic exemption limits of ₹ 3,00,000 and ₹ 5,00,000 apply **only to resident individuals** in India.\n* **Section 115BAC Opt-Out Requirement**: Assessee must exercise option to opt out of the default tax regime under Section 115BAC to avail these statutory slab structures.\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Health and Education Cess Standard Rate\n> Health and Education Cess is levied at a uniform rate of **4%** on the total Income Tax liability computed after applicable surcharges.",
